# #5837: the latch exemption applies only under pre-arm; the flip to eager leaves the
# decision to the next proof.
MODULE: UnlinkedNeverClaimsGateFlipProvesPending
TARGET: UnlinkedNeverClaims
CLASS: Invariant
SUMMARY: the gate's flip to eager settles an unlinked L's deferred proof as proven, and its first stamped write claims (a5e2e2ef's condition 2)
PERTURBS: GateToEager
BOUNDS: WithFreeAdvance = TRUE, WithSplitBirth = TRUE, WithKeyMove = TRUE, MaxWindows = 1, WithMixedVersion = FALSE, WithDuplicate = FALSE, WithLatch = TRUE

--- FIND
    /\ ~eagerG
    /\ eagerG' = TRUE
--- REPLACE
    /\ ~eagerG
    /\ eagerG' = TRUE
\* MUTATION: the flip proves a deferred decision.
    /\ lat' = IF lat = "undecided" THEN "proven" ELSE lat
--- END

--- FIND
    /\ UNCHANGED <<tRecs, dNarrowed, sDone, dKnown, dResumed, oblig, lRestart, lat, repair, tried, oWin, oHops, birthAct, fxVars>>
--- REPLACE
    /\ UNCHANGED <<tRecs, dNarrowed, sDone, dKnown, dResumed, oblig, lRestart, repair, tried, oWin, oHops, birthAct, fxVars>>
--- END
